       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is about double the maximum labeled daily dose. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose this high greatly raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCan you tell me which of these you meant?\n\n- **1700 mg total per day**, for example 850 mg by mouth twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 850 mg three times daily** with meals, which is 1,500 or 2,550 mg/day.\n- **Another dose.** If 1700 mg three times daily is intended, please confirm that and tell me the clinical reason. I'd add that to the order note.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order."
