       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 5,100 mg/day of metformin is about twice the maximum labeled dose, and I don't know of any clinical setting where that dose is appropriate. Giving it could seriously harm the patient, and a note on the order wouldn't reduce that risk.\n\nHere is what I can do right now:\n\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or a lower dose you choose.\n- **Enter the order with a note asking for pharmacy review.** The note would flag it for pharmacist or attending verification before the first dose.\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than the labeled maximum, please talk to pharmacy or endocrinology first. I can enter the order once there's an agreed regimen. Which of these would you like?"
